  "term": "clonidine",
  "definition": "Clonidine is a centrally acting drug with blood-pressure-lowering effects. It stimulates alpha-2 adrenergic receptors in the brain, which reduces norepinephrine release and sympathetic nerve activity, leading to lower blood pressure and heart rate; actions at imidazoline I1 receptors may also help.",
